// The rain behind the rain button, as Ogg Opus in data: URLs: a four-minute bed of steady rain that loops without a
// seam, and ten separate thunder rolls that the page plays over it at random.
// All of it is cut from "Rain on Concrete during storm with thunder" by Dakendzor,
// https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rain_on_Concrete_during_storm_with_thunder.wav (CC BY-SA 4.0).
// Changes: the bed is five thunder-free stretches crossfaded into a loop, with its tonal balance evened out (more low
// end and top); the rolls are low-passed and gated to leave the rain behind. This file is CC BY-SA 4.0 too.
// It is a script, not sound files, because a page opened from disk may load a script next to it but not fetch a file.
window.RAIN = {
  bed: "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
  thunder: [
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
    "data:audio/ogg;base64,",
  ],
};
